From bbe87baeef01bd8151b3a875f36000a08bd358b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Troy Sargent <0xalpharush@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:23:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(certify): prune scoped cut points to kept code

With external functions excluded, join points are cut only in the
functions the kept calls reach, and the EVM IR configuration graph
does not enter blocks only excluded functions run. Join relations pair
the edges a pass keeps (or the new block a split predecessor reaches)
instead of every predecessor pair, values a pass rematerializes from
calldata are related through the word they read, and segment proofs
let dsimp rewrite instances so the kernel accepts their terms.
---
